			<div class="content" id="post-content-4841651">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> SCP-XXX has no bodily orifices and all their skin is replaced with glass. The rest of them is hollow. They also possess regenerative capabilities, to the extent where they can regenerate 1/10th of their body in a minute. They were created in a glass factory explosion in Toulouse, France. They were formerly known as Georgine Lass. They were the only survivor. They have a strong hatred for transparent objects due to this, and will attempt to crack, break, or otherwise damage them when in line of sight. When exposed to even a very small amount of oxygen, they will engulf in flames reaching a temperature of 4000K. When this happens, they begin to run around erratically, usually burning though everything and everyone it comes close too.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Due to the severe flammability, all methods that foundation has thus far have been found not heat resistant enough, hence ineffective. It follows the logs of a pair of containment engineers working, getting pressured, mishaps, everything, as they try to create a containment chamber capable of containing them as they posed a severe containment risk and breached containment several times. They eventually do succeed.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> There will be 2 versions of the file, 1 before the success, and 1 after. The before one will have an O5 notice stating “All Containment Engineer Personal at Site X, unless told otherwise by a Foundation Employee with Level 4 Clearance or above, must focus all research, time, and resources to the creation of a containment chamber for SCP-XXX. The budget for containment has been increased to [Large Amount Of Site’s Local Currency].”</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> It's not just containment breaches 24/7, but more 1 monthly give or take. I will also have a recontainment procedure so it's not like it takes days to recontain.</p>

