<p>After a containment method that prevents them from catching fire is found, I would look at the mental toll this has had on them. This is where the glass will fit in, as they are continually reminded of what happened, how much of an abomination they are, and how many lives have been lost for her.</p>
<p>First, I think we have a slight miscommunication. The pair are focusing on how to create a better permanent containment that minimizes risk of containment breach, which eventually is achieved. I would have a private notes file at the bottom of the page with the story.</p>
<p>For the post permanent containment part, I was hoping to more focus on the mental toll, like I said earlier. I am thinking about some potential suicide attempts stopped by regenerative capabilities, but I'm still iffy on the suicide part.</p>
